h1. 11. Current Configuration Decision

The following configuration decision is currently implemented:

{panel:title=Current Configuration Decision|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#4C9AFF|bgColor=#DEEBFF}
DCP01 is configured as the Default Pool for the F5 Virtual Server.

The existing URI-based routing for DCP01, DCP02 and DCP03 remains unchanged.
{panel}

The change was introduced to address the PROD/DR automatic failover behavior observed when the Virtual Server did not have a Default Pool.

⸻

h1. 12. Important Limitation

The current configuration should not be interpreted as meaning that DCP01 represents the health of the complete DCP application.

For example:

{code}
DCP01 = UP
DCP02 = DOWN
DCP03 = DOWN
{code}

can still result in:

{code}
PROD VIP = UP
No site-level failover
{code}

because DCP01 remains healthy.

Therefore, the current design uses DCP01 as the primary availability reference for the Virtual Server but does not aggregate DCP01, DCP02 and DCP03 into a single application-health decision.

⸻

h1. 13. Future Validation Checklist

If the F5 configuration or failover architecture is changed in the future, validate the following behaviors.

|| Test || Expected Result ||
| DCP01, DCP02 and DCP03 healthy | PROD VIP remains available |
| All DCP01 members stopped | PROD VIP becomes unavailable and DR failover occurs |
| All DCP02 members stopped | DCP02 traffic impacted, but no site-level failover |
| All DCP03 members stopped | DCP03 traffic impacted, but no site-level failover |
| DCP02 and DCP03 stopped while DCP01 remains healthy | PROD VIP remains available |
| DCP01 stopped while DCP02 and DCP03 remain healthy | PROD to DR failover occurs |
| PROD unavailable and DR healthy | Traffic moves to DR |
| PROD restored | Validate expected failback behavior based on the configured F5 design |

