h1. 15. Final Summary

The DCP application uses URI-based routing behind an F5 Virtual Server for DCP01, DCP02 and DCP03.

Originally, no Default Pool was configured.

During active-active PROD/DR operation, automatic failover did not behave as expected.

The configuration was subsequently updated so that DCP01 is configured as the Default Pool.

The URI routing itself remains unchanged.

The key behavior of the current design is:

{panel:title=Current Failover Behavior|borderStyle=solid|borderColor=#36B37E|bgColor=#E3FCEF}
DCP01 DOWN
→ Default Pool unavailable
→ PROD VIP unavailable
→ PROD to DR failover

DCP02 DOWN and/or DCP03 DOWN while DCP01 remains UP
→ PROD VIP remains available
→ No overall site-level failover
{panel}

This document should be retained as the reference for the current F5 DCP PROD/DR configuration and failover behavior.

